    "https://unimelb.wd105.myworkdayjobs.com/UoM_External_Career/job/Parkville-Victoria/System-Specialist--Fee-Configuration_JR-017192-1": {
      "title": "System Specialist, Fee Configuration",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Number: JR-017192 Role type: Full-time; Continuing Department/School: Student and Learning Systems, Chief Operating Officer Portfolio Salary: UoM 7 - $111,275 - $120,453 p.a. plus 17% super Specialist tertiary fee configuration focus / shape compliant student fee processes across core systems / join a supportive, future-focused COO portfolio Apply now to leverage your fee configuration expertise, shape core student systems, and broaden your enterprise systems skills. Investing in you – 17% superannuation, benefits package including salary packaging, health and wellbeing programs, discounted services, and professional development opportunities. The University of Melbourne We take pride in our people, who all contribute to our mission to benefit society through the transformative impact of education and research. Discover more via our website. Your next career opportunity You will specialise in tertiary fee configuration, ensuring compliant, accurate fee structures across critical student systems, including StudentOne. You will work closely with Senior Domain Specialists to optimise processes, coordinate releases, and support peak operational periods. You will also broaden your remit, gaining experience across system access, triage, configuration, and vendor engagement. What you will deliver: Collaborate with Senior Domain Specialists to improve end-to-end student and learning processes and related system configurations. Specialise in tertiary fee configuration, translating policy and legislative requirements into accurate, maintainable system rules and refinements. Support system releases, including reviewing release notes, planning testing, and supporting business stakeholders through UAT activities. Manage system access and support operations through onboarding, offboarding, audits, and configuration required for peak periods. Triage and investigate support tickets, maintain documentation and knowledge bases, and contribute to backlog grooming and prioritisation. You may be a great fit if you: Have essential experience in tertiary fee configuration, including interpreting policy and legislation into practical system rules and structures. Offer hands-on expertise with StudentOne or similar student management systems within a complex tertiary education environment. Hold a relevant graduate qualification or equivalent combination of education and experience in technology-enabled business services. Demonstrate strong analytical skills, using evidence-based approaches to solve problems and optimise student and learning processes. Excel at triaging support tickets, organising backlogs, and coordinating stakeholders to meet agreed service levels. Navigate multiple systems and vendors confidently, balancing process thinking with technical configuration and collaborative delivery. For further information, please refer to the attached PD. What we offer you! We offer the opportunity to be part of a vibrant community and enjoy a comprehensive range of benefits to support your success and sense of fulfilment, including: Build future financial security with 17% superannuation Supportive flexible work arrangements underpinned by our commitment to inclusion and well-being Career development opportunities, including access to a range of tailored programs, such as Academic Women in Leadership, and learning platforms including LinkedIn Learning Progressive, considerate leave provisions to empower your work-life balance and well-being, including leading parental leave, gender affirmation leave and cultural leave Salary packaging and access to a range of discounted services including Bupa health insurance, and access to unique cultural and recreational benefits such as discounts for the Melbourne Theatre Company Health and well-being services including a leading Employee Assistance Program For more information check out our benefits page! Your new team Student and Learning Systems sits within the Chief Operating Officer Portfolio, supporting core student and learning technologies University-wide. As part of a collaborative, service-focused team, you will partner with business areas to enhance system performance. The team values continuous improvement, knowledge sharing and flexible working, offering strong support during peak operational periods. Be Yourself The University of Melbourne is an Equal Opportunity Employer and a child-safe organisation. The diversity of our community enriches us all, and we are committed to creating an inclusive and fair workplace where everyone is valued, respected, and empowered to succeed. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, identities, and experiences. Discover more about Diversity and Inclusion at UniMelb. We're committed to a barrier-free recruitment process and ongoing workplace support, providing adjustments throughout. We warmly encourage applications from people with disabilities. Learn more about how we support an accessible recruitment process. Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Applicants We aspire to be the University of choice for Indigenous Australians. Visit our Indigenous staff page to learn more about our investment and support for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander staff. Indigenous applicants are encouraged to connect with Korin Korin, our Indigenous Employment and Development team, via korin-korin@unimelb.edu.au Application essentials: Visit \"apply with us\" to learn more about the process, including tips and FAQs. You must have current valid work rights for Australia. Visa sponsorship is not available for this role. A Working with Children Check is required for all positions. If successful, we will guide you through the process and reimburse you. Please upload your resume and a cover letter outlining your interest and experience as part of the application process. Please upload a separate document addressing the Selection Criteria outlined in the Position Description. Want to know more? For questions related to our recruitment process email Mick Powar at hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au For recruitment adjustments contact Kim Groizard on +61 3 9035 3218 or at hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au (subject: 'Recruitment Adjustments'). Apply today, and join a community that’s shaping the future. Applications close: Monday 14th September at 11:55 PM; AEST Position Description: PD_JR-017192 System Specialist (Fee Configuration).pdf PD_JR-017192 System Specialist (Fee Configuration).docx"
    },
    "https://unimelb.wd105.myworkdayjobs.com/UoM_External_Career/job/Parkville/Head--International-House_JR-017860": {
      "title": "Head, International House",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nRole type:  Full-time, Continuing   Department:   Student and Scholarly Services –   Deputy Vice-Chancellor Education Portfolio   Salary:  Senior Manager   1   package   p.a.   including   17% super       Lead a globally minded residential college / shape transformative student experience / strengthen alumni and community engagement Apply now to lead International House’s residential community and elevate student wellbeing, belonging and academic success.   I nvesting in you   –   17% superannuation,   benefits package including salary packaging, health and wellbeing programs, discounted services, and professional development opportunities.       The University of Melbourne     We take pride in our people, who all contribute to our mission to   benefit   society through the transformative impact of education and research.   Discover more via our website .     Your next career opportunity     In this senior role, you will   shape the   academic and residential life at   International House .   You will   support   an inclusive, globally minded community   enabled   by   student wellbeing   and participation , belonging, leadership and academic achievement.   You will collaborate   with other Colleges and Halls and   with teams   across the University   to strengthen   partnerships,   alumni   engagement   and the overall residential   experience.     What you will deliver :     Lead a welcoming, inclusive residential community and design programmes that enhance   student   belonging, wellbeing,   success   and civic responsibility.   Oversee student welfare, pastoral care, incidents and risks, ensuring safe, supportive environments and compliance with relevant legislation.   Strengthen relationships with students, alumni, donors and partners, advancing reputation, engagement,   philanthropy   and community connections.   Provide inspirational leadership to staff and student leaders, overseeing operations, budgets,   contracts   and facilities improvements.   Develop and implement strategic and operational plans for International House, with clear KPIs and continuous improvement processes.     You may   be a great fit   if   you:     Hold   a relevant postgraduate qualification   and   demonstrate   substantial management   expertise , preferably   in   higher edu cation or other   complex   organisations .   Bring extensive experience in student accommodation or residential colleges, mentoring and supporting students’ academic and social wellbeing.   Demonstrate success developing and delivering strategic and operational plans, leading   continuous improvement initiatives.   Provide outstanding   people   leadership, building collaborative, high-performing teams and managing performance,   operations   and financial resources.   Excel at relationship-building,   consultation   and negotiation with diverse stakeholders, including executives, students,   alumni   and external partners.   Offer experience working with fundraising or advancement teams and, ideally, exposure to higher education environments.     For further   information   please refer to the attached PD .       What we offer you :   We offer the opportunity to be part of a vibrant community and enjoy a comprehensive range of benefits to support your success and sense of fulfilment, including:     Build future financial security with 17% superannuation. Supportive   work arrangements underpinned by our commitment to inclusion and well-being. Career development opportunities, including access to a range of tailored programs Progressive, considerate leave provisions to empower your work-life balance  and well-being, including leading parental leave, gender affirmation leave and cultural leave. Salary packaging and access to a range of discounted services including Bupa health insurance, and access to unique cultural and recreational benefits such as discounts for the Melbourne Theatre Company. Health and well-being services including a leading Employee Assistance Program.   For more information check out our benefits page!       Your new team – “ University Colleges and Residential Life ”     International House sits within the University Colleges and Residential Life portfolio in Student and Scholarly Services.   The portfolio unites University-owned colleges and halls to deliver residential experiences that foster wellbeing,   belonging   and success.   You will join a collaborative leadership group across residences and services to design inclusive, impactful communities and   programmes .   Together, you will   contribute to   Advancing Melbourne 2030 by enhancing student experience and strengthening alumni and community connections.     How to Apply:   Please upload your resume and a cover letter outlining your interest and experience, addressing the following   4   key selection criteria:   Extensive experience in student accommodation, residential life and colleges including in the mentoring and management of students, both for their academic advancement and their social wellbeing.   Demonstrated ability to develop and implement strategic and operational plans, and to   establish   and implement initiatives that enable successful execution of plans.    A strong   track record   of outstanding management and leadership skills, with   demonstrated   ability to foster a collaborative and cooperative work environment and develop high performing teams.    Proven ability to develop strong relationships and engage, collaborate,   consult   and negotiate with a broad group of internal and external stakeholders at all levels, from senior executives to undergraduate students.     Application essentials:   Visit   \"apply with us\"   to learn more about the process, including tips and FAQs.   You must have current valid work rights for Australia. Visa sponsorship is not available for this role.    A Working with Children Check is   required   for all positions. If successful, we will guide you through the process and reimburse you.     Want to know more?   For queries related to this specific position   or   recruitment process , contact   Susan Bradley   at susan.bradley@unimelb.edu.au For recruitment adjustments contact   Kim Groizard on +61 3 9035 3218   or at   hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au   (subject: 'Recruitment Adjustments').      Be Yourself     The University of Melbourne is an Equal Opportunity Employer and a child-safe organisation. The diversity of our community enriches us all, and we are committed to creating an inclusive and fair workplace where everyone is valued, respected, and empowered to succeed. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, identities, and experiences.   Discover more about Diversity and Inclusion at UniMelb.     We're   committed to a barrier-free recruitment process and ongoing workplace support, providing adjustments throughout. We warmly encourage applications from people with disabilities.   Learn more about how we support an accessible recruitment process .     Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Applicants     We aspire to be the University of choice for Indigenous Australians.   Visit   our   Indigenous staff page   to learn more about   our investment and support for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander staff.            Indigenous applicants are encouraged to connect with our Indigenous Employment & Development team at   korin-korin@unimelb.edu.au           Apply   today ,   and   join a community   that’s   shaping the future.     Applications close:   ​Sunday 13th September 2026 at   11:55 PM ;   Melbourne time zone.      Position Description:     PD - JR-017860 Head, International House.pdf"
    },
    "https://unimelb.wd105.myworkdayjobs.com/UoM_External_Career/job/Parkville/Director--Student-Administration_JR-017739": {
      "title": "Director, Student Administration",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted 6 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nRole type:  Full-time, Continuing   Department:  Student and Scholarly Services –   Deputy Vice-Chancellor Education Portfolio   Salary:  Senior Manager 2   package   p.a.   including   17% super     Shape an institution-wide student administration portfolio / lead transformative, data-informed services / influence exceptional experiences for diverse student cohorts .     Join us to lead a high-impact portfolio,   modernising   student services and shaping a sector-leading experience.   Investing in   you   –   17% superannuation,   benefits package including salary packaging, health and wellbeing programs, discounted services, and professional development opportunities.       The University of Melbourne     We take pride in our people, who all contribute to our mission to   benefit   society through the transformative impact of education and research.   Discover more via our website .     Your next career opportunity     This is a fantastic opportunity to make a positive impact on students   at   The University of Melbourne.   In this pivotal leadership role, you will   be responsible for   University -wide student administration across the full enrolment lifecycle.   You will drive service innovation, technology-enabled transformation, and continuous improvement that measurably enhances student and staff experiences. You will influence strategy, partner with senior   leaders   and lead a large, skilled team to deliver exceptional outcomes.     What   you will   deliver :     Lead end-to-end student administrative services, ensuring high-quality,   timely , and consistent support across the entire student lifecycle.   Develop and execute strategy for student administration, informed by stakeholder feedback, benchmarking and best-practice standards across the sector.   Build and lead a high-performing, future-ready workforce through effective planning, capability development, performance   management   and succession strategies.   Drive    transformation   and service innovation, optimising processes,   channels   and technologies to improve experience and efficiency.   Ensure robust governance, compliance,   reporting   and risk management for student administration, including business ownership of key enterprise systems.     You may   be a great fit   if   you:     Hold a relevant graduate qualification and extensive leadership experience in complex, multi-stakeholder organisations, preferably higher education.   Demonstrate   leadership of shared services and service   optimisation , with a focus on improving efficiency,   quality   and staff capability.    Have strong experience in leading change management and continuous improvement initiatives in highly regulated settings, with   demonstrated   ability to reduce risk and deliver positive outcomes.   Have a   track-record   of driving technology and service innovation initiatives that   improve   access,   efficiency   and compliance. This includes initiatives that deliver measurable efficiencies or customer improvements.   Have a proven ability to   translate strategy into   prioritised   work   programmes   with robust governance and measurable outcomes.   Have deep experience in building and   maintaining   effective working relationships and buy-in with senior stakeholders through influential engagement.     For further   information   please refer to the attached PD .       What we offer you :   We offer the opportunity to be part of a vibrant community and enjoy a comprehensive range of benefits to support your success and sense of fulfilment, including:     Build future financial security with 17% superannuation. Supportive   work arrangements underpinned by our commitment to inclusion and well-being  . Career development opportunities, including access to a range of tailored programs. Progressive, considerate leave provisions to empower your work-life balance  and well-being, including leading parental leave, gender affirmation leave and cultural leave. Salary packaging and access to a range of discounted services including Bupa health insurance, and access to unique cultural and recreational benefits such as discounts for the Melbourne Theatre Company. Health and well-being services including a leading Employee Assistance Program. For more information check out our benefits page!       Your new team – “ Student Administration ”     Student Administration sits within Student and Scholarly Services, part of the Deputy Vice-Chancellor (Education) portfolio.      We enable high-quality, end-to-end services that support students from first enquiry through to graduation and beyond. Our teams collaborate closely with faculties,   schools   and Chancellery to deliver consistent, student- centred   administrative experiences.   We value mission focus, service   excellence   and working better together to continually improve how we support our community. As part of this leadership group, you will shape strategy,   culture   and innovation across the University-wide portfolio.     How to Apply:   Please upload your resume and a cover letter outlining your interest and experience, addressing the following 3 key selection criteria:   Demonstrated leadership of shared services and service   optimisation , with a focus on improving efficiency,   quality   and staff capability. This includes developing staff to their full potential and effectively managing staff performance.   Experience in leading   transformative change   and continuous improvement initiatives in highly regulated settings, with   demonstrated   ability to reduce risk and deliver positive outcomes.   Drive technology and service innovation   initiatives that   improves   access,   efficiency   and compliance. This includes initiatives that   delivered   measurable efficiencies or customer improvements.     Application essentials:   Visit   \"apply with us\"   to learn more about the process, including tips and FAQs.   You must have current valid work rights for Australia. Visa sponsorship is not available for this role.    A Working with Children Check is   required   for all positions. If successful, we will guide you through the process and reimburse you.     Want to know more?   For queries related to this specific position   or   recruitment process , contact   Susan Bradley   at   susan.bradley@unimelb.edu.au   For recruitment adjustments contact   Kim Groizard on +61 3 9035 3218   or at   hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au   (subject: 'Recruitment Adjustments').      Be Yourself     The University of Melbourne is an Equal Opportunity Employer and a child-safe organisation. The diversity of our community enriches us all, and we are committed to creating an inclusive and fair workplace where everyone is valued, respected, and empowered to succeed. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, identities, and experiences.   Discover more about Diversity and Inclusion at UniMelb.     We're   committed to a barrier-free recruitment process and ongoing workplace support, providing adjustments throughout. We warmly encourage applications from people with disabilities.   Learn more about how we support an accessible recruitment process .     Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Applicants     We aspire to be the University of choice for Indigenous Australians.   Visit   our   Indigenous staff page   to learn more about   our investment and support for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander staff.     Indigenous applicants are encouraged to connect with our Indigenous Employment & Development team at   korin-korin@unimelb.edu.au         Apply   today ,   and   join a community   that’s   shaping the future.     Applications close:   ​Sunday 13th September 2026 at   11:55 PM ;   Melbourne time zone.      Position Description: PD - JR-017739 Director, Student Administration.docx PD - JR-017739 Director, Student Administration.pdf"
    },
