    "https://unimelb.wd105.myworkdayjobs.com/UoM_External_Career/job/Parkville/Professor-of-Accounting--Fitzgerald-Chair-_JR-014983-2": {
      "title": "Professor of Accounting (Fitzgerald Chair)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-11\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nRole type:  Full-time; Continuing Faculty:  Business and Economics Department:  Accounting Salary:  Level E - an attractive remuneration package will be offered plus 17% super   Prestigious Fitzgerald Chair honouring pioneering accounting scholars / Lead globally recognised research, education and policy influence / Shape profession, regulators and industry partnership Apply now to become the Fitzgerald Chair and drive impactful accounting research, teaching and public engagement. Investing in you – 17% superannuation, benefits package including salary packaging, health and wellbeing programs, discounted services, and professional development opportunities.    The University of Melbourne   We take pride in our people, who all contribute to our mission to benefit society through the transformative impact of education and research. Discover more via our website.   Your next career opportunity   In this esteemed professorial role, you will lead globally recognised research and innovative teaching in accounting. You will shape public debate, influence policy and mentor the next generation of scholars and practitioners, while providing strategic leadership within a highly respected Department and Faculty.   What you will deliver:   Lead an ambitious research agenda in accounting, publishing in top-tier international journals and other scholarly outlets. Secure competitive external research funding and foster collaborative projects with national and international partners. Provide inspiring leadership in teaching across undergraduate and graduate programmes, including curriculum innovation and enhancement. Supervise and mentor doctoral and honours students, building a strong, supportive research training culture. Contribute actively to boards, committees and professional forums, strengthening the Department’s profile with regulators, government and industry.   You may be a great fit if you:   Hold a PhD in accounting or a closely related discipline. Demonstrate an outstanding record of impactful publications in leading international accounting journals. Provide evidence of successful, innovative teaching at both undergraduate and graduate levels. Lead and mentor academic colleagues and graduate researchers towards shared excellence and impact. Build strong, enduring relationships with regulators, standard setters, government and industry partners. Secure or contribute to competitive external research funding and major collaborative research initiatives.   For further information please refer to the attached PD.    What we offer you!   We offer the opportunity to be part of a vibrant community and enjoy a comprehensive range of benefits to support your success and sense of fulfilment, including:  Build future financial security with 17% superannuation Supportive flexible work arrangements underpinned by our commitment to inclusion and well-being. Career development opportunities, including access to a range of tailored programs, such as Academic Women in Leadership, and learning platforms including LinkedIn Learning. Progressive, considerate leave provisions to empower your work-life balance and well-being, including leading parental leave, gender affirmation leave and cultural leave. Salary packaging and access to a range of discounted services including Bupa health insurance, and access to unique cultural and recreational benefits such as discounts for the Melbourne Theatre Company. Health and well-being services including a leading Employee Assistance Program.   For more information check out our benefits page!    Your new team – “Department of Accounting”   You will join the Department of Accounting, a dynamic community of over 40 academics delivering research, teaching and engagement across financial and managerial accounting, auditing and assurance, and accounting information systems. As part of the Faculty of Business and Economics, you will work within a globally respected business school with strong industry, government and professional networks. You will benefit from a collegial, research-intensive environment that values innovation, impact and the development of future leaders in accounting.   Be Yourself   The University of Melbourne is an Equal Opportunity Employer and a child-safe organisation. The diversity of our community enriches us all, and we are committed to creating an inclusive and fair workplace where everyone is valued, respected, and empowered to succeed. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, identities, and experiences. Discover more about Diversity and Inclusion at UniMelb.   We're committed to a barrier-free recruitment process and ongoing workplace support, providing adjustments throughout. We warmly encourage applications from people with disabilities. Learn more about how we support an accessible recruitment process.   Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Applicants   We aspire to be the University of choice for Indigenous Australians. Visit our Indigenous staff page to learn more about our investment and support for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander staff.    Indigenous applicants are encouraged to connect with our Indigenous Employment & Development team at korin-korin@unimelb.edu.au     Application essentials: Visit \"apply with us\" to learn more about the process, including tips and FAQs. You must have current valid work rights for Australia. Visa sponsorship is not available for this role. A Working with Children Check is required for all positions. If successful, we will guide you through the process and reimburse you. Please upload your responses to the Selection Criteria, found in the Position Description.   Want to know more? For queries related to this specific position, contact Professor Brad Potter at the details in the position description. For questions related to our recruitment process email Shabon Nawabi at hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au For recruitment adjustments contact Kim Groizard on +61 3 9035 3218 or at hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au (subject: 'Recruitment Adjustments').   Apply today, and join a community that’s shaping the future.   Applications close: Sunday 11th October 11:55 PM; Melbourne time zone.    Position Description:   PD - JR-014983 Professor of Accounting (Fitzgerald Chair).docx PD - JR-014983 Professor of Accounting (Fitzgerald Chair).pdf"
    },
    "https://unimelb.wd105.myworkdayjobs.com/UoM_External_Career/job/Parkville/Category-Manager_JR-017617-1": {
      "title": "Category Manager",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-11\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nPosition Number:   JR-017617   Role type:   Full Time; Continuing   Location:   Parkville   Department/School:   Chief Financial Officer Group – Procurement Services   Salary:   UoM 8 .5   -   $135,504 p.a. plus 17% super   Strategic, University-wide procurement remit / drive sustainable, socially responsible sourcing and modern slavery risk management / join a high-performing, evolving CFO team   Seize this opportunity to lead complex category strategies, deliver measurable   value   and shape   sustainable procurement.   Investing in you – 17% superannuation, benefits package including salary packaging, health and wellbeing programs, discounted services, and professional development opportunities.        The University of Melbourne   We take pride in our people, who all contribute to our mission to   benefit   society through the transformative impact of education and research.   Discover more via our website.   Your next career opportunity     In this role, you will lead University-wide category strategies and complex sourcing projects that deliver significant value. You will partner with senior stakeholders to shape sustainable, socially responsible procurement,   strengthening   vendor   performance   and   managing   risk. You will also develop your   expertise   within a high-performing CFO Group committed to culture,   learning   and innovation.   What you will deliver:     Lead multiple   complex ,   University-wide IT sourcing projects, f rom strategy and market engagement   through to   recommendation and contracting.   Develop and implement category management plans with stakeholders to   maximise   value and manage risk across categories.   Partner with senior leaders and COO portfolios to align renewals, priorities, strategies and ensure compliance and probity.   Guide   stakeholders through procurement processes, negotiations, vendor performance   management   and sustainable, socially responsible sourcing practices.   Monitor category performance, resolve issues, benchmark best   practice   and contribute to financial, sustainability and modern slavery goals.   You may be a great fit if you:     Hold a relevant undergraduate qualification or equivalent experience in procurement and   contracts   management.   Bring 5–8 years’ experience delivering complex sourcing projects and achieving strong commercial and financial outcomes.   Demonstrate advanced tender development,   evaluation   and negotiation skills within diverse strategic or large, complex environments.   Analyse   complex data sets to generate insights that inform category strategies and value-for-money decisions.   Operate independently under broad direction, managing competing priorities across multiple University-wide procurement activities.   Apply knowledge of Australian Procurement Standards and social, sustainable procurement, including modern slavery risk management.   For further information, please refer to the attached PD.     What we offer you!     We offer the opportunity to be part of a vibrant community and enjoy a comprehensive range of benefits to support your success and sense of fulfilment, including:    Build future financial security with 17% superannuation   Supportive flexible work arrangements underpinned by our commitment to inclusion and well-being    Career development opportunities, including access to a range of tailored programs, such as Academic Women in Leadership, and learning platforms including LinkedIn Learning   Progressive, considerate leave provisions to empower your work-life balance and well-being, including leading parental leave, gender affirmation leave and cultural leave   Salary packaging and access to a range of discounted services including Bupa health insurance, and access to unique cultural and recreational benefits such as discounts for the Melbourne Theatre Company    Health and well-being services including a leading Employee Assistance Program    For more information check out our benefits page!     Your new team   Your new team sits within the Chief Financial Officer Group, part of the Chief Operating Officer Portfolio. We provide   the financial   and procurement   expertise   that underpins exceptional teaching,   research   and student experiences across the University.   You will join a procurement team investing in culture and high performance, with access to development programs and cross-University collaborations that drive sustainable, value-for-money outcomes.   Be Yourself     The University of Melbourne is an Equal Opportunity Employer and a child-safe   organisation . The diversity of our community enriches us all, and we are committed to creating an inclusive and fair workplace where everyone is valued, respected, and empowered to succeed. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, identities, and experiences.   Discover more about Diversity and Inclusion at UniMelb.   We're   committed to a barrier-free recruitment process and ongoing workplace support, providing adjustments throughout. We warmly encourage applications from people with disabilities.   Learn more about how we support an accessible recruitment process.   Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Applicants     We aspire to be the University of choice for Indigenous Australians. Visit   our   Indigenous staff page   to learn more about our investment and support for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander staff.     Indigenous applicants are encouraged to connect with Korin   Korin , our Indigenous Employment and Development team, via   korin-korin@unimelb.edu.au   Application essentials:   Visit   \"apply with us\"   to learn more about the process, including tips and FAQs.   You must have current valid work rights for Australia. Visa sponsorship is not available for this role.    A Working with Children Check is   required   for all positions. If successful, we will guide you through the process and reimburse you.    Please upload your   resume and a cover letter   outlining your interest and experience as part of the application process.     Want to know more?   For questions related to our recruitment process email   Tien Nguyen   at   hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au   For recruitment adjustments contact Kim Groizard on +61 3 9035 3218 or at   hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au   (subject: 'Recruitment Adjustments').    Apply   today, and   join a community   that’s   shaping the future.   Applications close :   Tuesday, 16th September 2026 at   11:55 PM; Melbourne time zone.    Position Description:   PD_JR-017617 Category Manager.docx   PD_JR-017617 Category Manager.pdf"
    },
    "https://unimelb.wd105.myworkdayjobs.com/UoM_External_Career/job/Clinical-Sites-Metro--Regional/Executive-Assistant_JR-017303": {
      "title": "Executive Assistant",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-10\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nRole type: Fixed Term for 12 months; 0.6FTE   Faculty: Medicine, Dentistry and Health Sciences   Department: Department of Medicine – Austin Health   Salary: $ 86,943 - $99,864 p.a. plus 17% super    Unique opportunity to support a globally renowned clinician-scientist / central role in epilepsy research and patient care / dynamic multidisciplinary environment at the Melbourne Brain Centre .   Apply now to play a pivotal support role enabling impactful clinical care and breakthrough epilepsy research.   Investing in you – 17% superannuation, benefits package including salary packaging, health and wellbeing programs, discounted services, and professional development opportunities.      The University of Melbourne   We take pride in our people, who all contribute to our mission to benefit society through the transformative impact of education and research. Discover more via our website.   Your next career opportunity   In this Executive Assistant role, you will support Laureate Professor Ingrid Scheffer across clinical, research and leadership responsibilities.   You will coordinate complex clinic operations and research activities, ensuring outstanding patient care and advancing epilepsy understanding.   You will build strong relationships across hospital, university and external partners while refining high-level executive support skills.   What you will deliver:     Coordinate multidisciplinary clinic schedules, appointments and logistics to support efficient, patient-centred epilepsy care.   Prepare and manage patient files, clinical documentation and records to ensure accuracy, completeness and timely access. Facilitate clear communication between clinicians, patients, hospital departments, healthcare services and external organisations.   Provide high-level executive support including correspondence, diary management, meetings, travel arrangements and related logistics .   Uphold strict confidentiality and compliance with healthcare, privacy and organisational policies across all activities.       You may be a great fit if you :     Hold a tertiary qualification or equivalent experience and specialist expertise in administrative or executive support fields.   Bring proven experience supporting senior executives, managing complex diaries, meetings and competing priorities.   Demonstrate strong time management skills, coordinating workflows, meeting deadlines and balancing concurrent clinical and research tasks.   Display excellent interpersonal communication, building relationships with clinicians, academics, administrative staff and external stakeholders.   Exercise diplomacy, tact and discretion, confidently handling sensitive information and maintaining strict confidentiality.   Deliver high-quality written correspondence, briefing papers and presentations with exceptional attention to detail and literacy.   For further information , please refer to the attached PD.     What we offer you!   We offer the opportunity to be part of a vibrant community and enjoy a comprehensive range of benefits to support your success and sense of fulfilment, including:    Build future financial security with 17% superannuation .   Supportive flexible work arrangements underpinned by our commitment to inclusion and well-being .     Career development opportunities, including access to a range of tailored programs, such as Academic Women in Leadership, and learning platforms including LinkedIn Learning .   Progressive, considerate leave provisions to empower your work-life balance and well-being, including leading parental leave, gender affirmation leave and cultural leave .   Salary packaging and access to a range of discounted services including Bupa health insurance, and access to unique cultural and recreational benefits such as discounts for the Melbourne Theatre Company .     Health and well-being services including a leading Employee Assistance Program .       For more information check out our benefits page!   Your new team –   At the Melbourne Brain Centre on the Austin Health campus, you will join a vibrant, multidisciplinary environment.   Clinicians, researchers and professional staff collaborate to improve outcomes for children with epilepsy and neurological disorders.   The team embraces innovation, creativity and evidence-based practice, supported by the University of Melbourne’s strong research culture.   Values of collaboration, compassion, respect, integrity and accountability shape everyday interactions and decision-making.   You will be supported to develop your career and wellbeing while contributing to impactful clinical care and research .   Be Yourself   The University of Melbourne is an Equal Opportunity Employer and a child-safe organisation . The diversity of our community enriches us all, and we are committed to creating an inclusive and fair workplace where everyone is valued, respected, and empowered to succeed. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, identities, and experiences. Discover more about Diversity and Inclusion at UniMelb .   We're committed to a barrier-free recruitment process and ongoing workplace support, providing adjustments throughout. We warmly encourage applications from people with disabilities. Learn more about how we support an accessible recruitment process .   Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Applicants   We aspire to be the University of choice for Indigenous Australians. Visit our Indigenous staff page to learn more about our investment and support for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander staff.        Indigenous applicants are encouraged to connect with our Indigenous Employment & Development team at korin-korin@unimelb.edu.au .    Application essentials:   Visit \"apply with us\" to learn more about the process, including tips and FAQs.   You must have current valid work rights for Australia. Visa sponsorship is not available for this role.    A Working with Children Check is required for all positions. If successful, we will guide you through the process and reimburse you.    Please upload your resume and a cover letter outlining your interest and experience as part of the application process.    Please upload your responses to the Selection Criteria, found in the Position Description.      Want to know more?   For queries related to this specific position, contact Walid by emailing walid.abdullatif@unimelb.edu.au   For questions related to our recruitment process email Walid at hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au   For recruitment adjustments contact Kim Groizard on +61 3 9035 3218 or at hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au (subject: 'Recruitment Adjustments').      Apply today and join a community that’s shaping the future.   Applications close: 24 September 11:55 PM; Melbourne time zone.    Position Description:     JR-017303 Executive Assistant PD.pdf JR-017303 Executive Assistant PD.doc"
    },
    "https://unimelb.wd105.myworkdayjobs.com/UoM_External_Career/job/Parkville/Manager--Public-Health-Programs_JR-017953": {
      "title": "Manager, Public Health Programs",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-10\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nRole type: Full-time; Fixed term 2 years   Faculty: Medicine, Dentistry and Health Sciences   Department/School: Department of Microbiology and Immunology, Doherty Institute   Salary: UOM 8: $125,191 - $135,504 p.a. plus 17% super     High-impact national public health role / lead and manage genomics programmes with Australian CDC and health departments / collaborate across Australia and Asia-Pacific   Apply now to lead coordinated public health initiatives that enhance surveillance systems and strengthen national preparedness.   Investing in you – 17% superannuation, benefits package including salary packaging, health and wellbeing programs, discounted services, and professional development opportunities.      The University of Melbourne   We take pride in our people, who all contribute to our mission to benefit society through the transformative impact of education and research. Discover more via our website.   Your next career opportunity:   You will manage flagship public health programmes across MDU PHL and the Centre for Pathogen Genomics. You will coordinate AusPathoGen , CDGN and related networks to embed pathogen genomics into national surveillance and response.   You will engage Australian CDC, health departments and regional partners, shaping impactful public health policy and practice.   What you will deliver:   Lead planning and delivery of public health initiatives, including workplans, governance structures, documentation and strategic funding opportunities.   Manage relationships with Australian CDC, Commonwealth and state health departments, funders and public health networks.   Coordinate multidisciplinary teams to deliver complex projects, organising meetings, workshops, technical activities and high-quality reporting outputs.   Oversee programme compliance with funding agreements, including reporting, evaluation, budgeting, finance tracking and communication requirements.   Support grant applications, stakeholder engagement and supervision of project management staff to expand public health activities.     You may be a great fit if you:   Hold tertiary qualification and experience in public health or a closely related discipline.   Demonstrate success managing large-scale public health projects with complex, multi-jurisdictional stakeholder environments.   Build effective relationships with government agencies, health departments and public health networks to progress shared objectives .   Apply advanced organisational and project management skills, delivering detailed workplans, timelines and monitored implementation.   Produce high-quality briefings, reports, proposals and public-facing communications tailored to diverse stakeholder audiences.   Use strong analytical, problem-solving and Microsoft Office skills to support data-driven programme decisions.   For further information please refer to the attached PD.    What we offer you!   We offer the opportunity to be part of a vibrant community and enjoy a comprehensive range of benefits to support your success and sense of fulfilment, including:    Build future financial security with 17% superannuation   Supportive flexible work arrangements underpinned by our commitment to inclusion and well-being    Career development opportunities, including access to a range of tailored programs, such as Academic Women in Leadership, and learning platforms including LinkedIn Learning   Progressive, considerate leave provisions to empower your work-life balance and well-being, including leading parental leave, gender affirmation leave and cultural leave   Salary packaging and access to a range of discounted services including Bupa health insurance, and access to unique cultural and recreational benefits such as discounts for the Melbourne Theatre Company    Health and well-being services including a leading Employee Assistance Program    For more information check out our benefits page!   Your new team – Department of Microbiology and Immunology   You will join the Department of Microbiology and Immunology, part of the School of Biomedical Sciences. MDU PHL is a century-old, NATA-accredited public health laboratory leading diagnostics, reference services and pathogen genomics.   You will collaborate with experts across genomics, epidemiology and bioinformatics, working on programmes with national and regional impact.   Our culture values collaboration, compassion, respect, integrity and accountability, while supporting your development and wellbeing.   Be Yourself   The University of Melbourne is an Equal Opportunity Employer and a child-safe organisation. The diversity of our community enriches us all, and we are committed to creating an inclusive and fair workplace where everyone is valued, respected, and empowered to succeed. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, identities, and experiences. Discover more about Diversity and Inclusion at UniMelb .   We're committed to a barrier-free recruitment process and ongoing workplace support, providing adjustments throughout. We warmly encourage applications from people with disabilities. Learn more about how we support an accessible recruitment process .   Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Applicants   We aspire to be the University of choice for Indigenous Australians. Visit our Indigenous staff page to learn more about our investment and support for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander staff.        Indigenous applicants are encouraged to connect with our Indigenous Employment & Development team at korin-korin@unimelb.edu.au .    Application essentials:   Visit \"apply with us\" to learn more about the process, including tips and FAQs.   You must have current valid work rights for Australia. Visa sponsorship is not available for this role.    A Working with Children Check is required for all positions. If successful, we will guide you through the process and reimburse you.    Please upload your resume and a cover letter outlining your interest and experience as part of the application process.    Please upload your responses to the Selection Criteria, found in the Position Description.      Want to know more?   For questions related to our recruitment process email hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au   For recruitment adjustments contact Kim Groizard on +61 3 9035 3218 or at hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au (subject: 'Recruitment Adjustments').    Apply today, and join a community that’s shaping the future.   Applications close: Wednesday 23 September at 11:55 PM; Melbourne time zone.    Position Description: PD_Manager, Public Health Programs.docx"
    },
    "https://unimelb.wd105.myworkdayjobs.com/UoM_External_Career/job/Parkville/Associate-Professor-in-Periodontics_JR-009367-1": {
      "title": "Professor in Periodontics",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-10\nPosted: Posted 4 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nRole type:  Part-time (0.8 FTE) to Full-time; Continuing Faculty:  Medicine, Dentistry and Health Sciences School:  Melbourne Dental School Salary: Level D: AUD $183,859 - $202,556 p.a.              Level E: AUD $236,824 p.a.              plus 17% super and clinical loading of AUD $13,494 p.a. International leadership in specialist Periodontics / Shape a nationally benchmarked Doctor of Clinical Dentistry (DCD) Periodontics program / Drive impactful translational research Join us to lead specialist Periodontics education, research and clinical innovation that advances oral health globally. Investing in you – 17% superannuation, benefits package including salary packaging, health and wellbeing programs, discounted services, and professional development opportunities.  The University of Melbourne   We take pride in our people, who all contribute to our mission to benefit society through the transformative impact of education and research. Discover more via our website. Your next career opportunity   You will lead the Doctor of Clinical Dentistry (DCD) Periodontics program, integrating specialist clinical training, cutting-edge research and curriculum innovation. You will shape national and international standards in Periodontics while mentoring the next generation of specialist clinicians. What you will deliver:   Lead the design, delivery and evaluation of the DCD Periodontics curriculum and assessment across clinical and academic components. Provide high-quality clinical supervision and safe patient care at RDHM, modelling evidence-based, multidisciplinary specialist Periodontics practice. Establish and lead an internationally recognised research program in Periodontics, securing competitive funding and collaborative partnerships. Supervise and mentor higher degree and postgraduate research students, building research capacity across the discipline and School. Provide strategic leadership in national curriculum frameworks, accreditation standards and professional guidelines for specialist Periodontics. You may be a great fit if you:   Hold and maintain current or clearly eligible specialist AHPRA registration in Periodontics, without limiting conditions or restrictions. Possess a completed PhD in Periodontics or a closely related field, with strong academic credentials. Demonstrate strategic leadership in specialist clinical teaching, including curriculum design, assessment, benchmarking and educational innovation. Show a sustained record of high-quality research, including competitive grant success and impactful translational outcomes. Bring extensive experience supervising higher degree and postgraduate research students through to successful thesis completion. Engage confidently with national and international professional bodies, accreditation panels and multidisciplinary clinical partners. For further information please refer to the attached Candidate Information Pack .  What we offer you!   We offer the opportunity to be part of a vibrant community and enjoy a comprehensive range of benefits to support your success and sense of fulfilment, including:  Build future financial security with 17% superannuation Supportive flexible work arrangements underpinned by our commitment to inclusion and well-being  Career development opportunities, including access to a range of tailored programs, such as Academic Women in Leadership, and learning platforms including LinkedIn Learning Progressive, considerate leave provisions to empower your work-life balance and well-being, including leading parental leave, gender affirmation leave and cultural leave Salary packaging and access to a range of discounted services including Bupa health insurance, and access to unique cultural and recreational benefits such as discounts for the Melbourne Theatre Company  Health and well-being services including a leading Employee Assistance Program  For more information check out our benefits page!  Your new team – “Melbourne Dental School”   You will join the Melbourne Dental School, a leader in specialist dental education and translational research. Working closely with the Royal Dental Hospital of Melbourne, you will help deliver world-class patient-centred clinical training. You will collaborate in a values-driven Faculty of Medicine, Dentistry and Health Sciences, committed to Advancing Health 2030. Be Yourself   The University of Melbourne is an Equal Opportunity Employer and a child-safe organisation. The diversity of our community enriches us all, and we are committed to creating an inclusive and fair workplace where everyone is valued, respected, and empowered to succeed. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, identities, and experiences. Discover more about Diversity and Inclusion at UniMelb. We're committed to a barrier-free recruitment process and ongoing workplace support, providing adjustments throughout. We warmly encourage applications from people with disabilities. Learn more about how we support an accessible recruitment process. Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Applicants   We aspire to be the University of choice for Indigenous Australians. Visit our Indigenous staff page to learn more about our investment and support for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander staff.    Indigenous applicants are encouraged to connect with our Indigenous Employment & Development team at korin-korin@unimelb.edu.au   Application essentials: Visit \"apply with us\" to learn more about the process, including tips and FAQs. You must have current valid work rights for Australia. Visa sponsorship is not available for this role. A Working with Children Check is required for all positions. If successful, we will guide you through the process and reimburse you. Please upload your responses to the Selection Criteria, found in the Position Description. Want to know more? For queries related to this specific position, contact Professor Petros Papagerakis or Professor Ivan Darby at the details listed in the position description. For questions related to our recruitment process email Shabon Nawabi at hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au For recruitment adjustments contact Kim Groizard on +61 3 9035 3218 or at hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au (subject: 'Recruitment Adjustments'). Apply today, and join a community that’s shaping the future. Applications close: Friday 9th October 11:55 PM; Melbourne time zone.  Position Description:   Candidate Information Pack - Professor in Periodontics.pdf"
    },
    "https://unimelb.wd105.myworkdayjobs.com/UoM_External_Career/job/Dookie/Assistant-Farm-Hand_JR-018015": {
      "title": "Assistant Farm Hand",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-09\nPosted: Posted 5 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nRole type:   Full time; Fixed Term   for 12 months   Fa c ulty :   Faculty of Science   Department / School:   School of Agriculture, Food and Ecosystem Sciences   Salary:   UOM 2:   $6 6 , 493   - $6 9 ,1 82   p.a. plus 17% super     Gain hands-on experience in livestock and cropping while building essential agricultural skills.   Apply now to join a dynamic farm team and contribute to agricultural education and research.   Investing in   you -   benefits package including salary packaging, health and wellbeing programs, discounted services, and professional development opportunities.     The University of Melbourne     We take pride in our people, who all contribute to our mission to   benefit   society through the transformative impact of education and research.   Discover more via our website .   Your next career opportunity     Join the University of Melbourne's Dookie Campus as an Assistant Farm Hand, where   you'll   play a vital role in supporting the day-to-day operations of the campus's livestock enterprises and   assisting   with broadacre cropping activities. This hands-on position offers an excellent opportunity to develop practical skills in livestock husbandry, crop management, and farm operations while contributing to the university's agricultural education and research initiatives.   What you will deliver:     Livestock Operations: Assist the Farm Hand and Farm Manager with basic day-to-day operations of the livestock enterprises, including feeding animals, managing sheep flocks (weighing, yarding, and shearing), and   assisting   with the robotic dairy operations   and   a ssist   with spraying weeds, fence maintenance .   Farm Maintenance: Assist the Farm Hand with routine maintenance and repairs, ensuring responsible use of farm machinery and equipment.   Record Management: Assist the Farm Manager with   accurate   management of farm records.   Animal Husbandry:   Participate   in key animal husbandry tasks, adhering to best practices in livestock management.   You may be a great fit you:     Are a practical and hands-on individual with a keen interest in agriculture, possessing a willingness to learn and contribute to farm operations while working collaboratively in a team environment.   Have experience in basic livestock husbandry tasks, such as feeding, weighing, and handling animals.   Possess knowledge of farm machinery and equipment operation and maintenance.   Demonstrate a commitment to safe work practices and adherence to occupational health and safety guidelines.   Exhibit strong attention to detail and the ability to follow instructions accurately.   Be physically fit and able to perform manual   labour   tasks as   required .   Possess a willingness to learn and contribute to continuous improvement initiatives.   Be an effective team player with   strong communication   and interpersonal skills.   For further   information   please refer to the attached PD.     What we offer you!     We offer the opportunity to be part of a vibrant community and enjoy a comprehensive range of benefits to support your success and sense of fulfilment, including:    Build future financial security with 17% superannuation   Supportive flexible work arrangements underpinned by our commitment to inclusion and well-being    Career development opportunities, including access to a range of tailored programs, such as Academic Women in Leadership, and learning platforms including LinkedIn Learning   Progressive, considerate leave provisions to empower your work-life balance and well-being, including leading parental leave, gender affirmation leave and cultural leave   Salary packaging and access to a range of discounted services including Bupa health insurance, and access to unique cultural and recreational benefits such as discounts for the Melbourne Theatre Company    Health and well-being services including a leading Employee Assistance Program    For more information check out our benefits page!     Your new team –   School of Agriculture, Food and Ecosystem Sciences   The School of Agriculture, Food and Ecosystem Sciences (SAFES) has a vision of flourishing environments and communities. It brings together diverse discipline strengths to lead the development of new interdisciplinary thinking and high-impact solutions for global challenges relating to climate change, food security, healthy food systems, biodiversity conservation, sustainable forest management, invasive species, and environmentally and economically sustainable agricultural practices.   The faculty of science is home to seven schools: Agriculture, Food & Ecosystem Sciences; Biosciences; Chemistry; Geography, Earth & Atmospheric Sciences; Mathematics & Statistics; Physics; and Melbourne Veterinary School. Science at Melbourne is a global leader across discovery and applied scientific research and education. Science begins with curiosity, and we are dedicated to understanding the universe from the level of sub-atomic particles to the solar system.   Be Yourself     The University of Melbourne is an Equal Opportunity Employer and a child-safe   organisation . The diversity of our community enriches us all, and we are committed to creating an inclusive and fair workplace where everyone is valued, respected, and empowered to succeed. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, identities, and experiences.   Discover more about Diversity and Inclusion at UniMelb.   We're   committed to a barrier-free recruitment process and ongoing workplace support, providing adjustments throughout. We warmly encourage applications from people with disabilities.   Learn more about how we support an accessible recruitment process .   Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Applicants     We aspire to be the University of choice for Indigenous Australians.   Visit   our   Indigenous staff page   to learn more about our investment and support for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander staff.            Indigenous applicants are encouraged to connect with our Indigenous Employment & Development team at   oied-hr@unimelb.edu.au .    Application essentials:   Visit   \"apply with us\"   to learn more about the process, including tips and FAQs.   You must have current valid work rights for Australia. Visa sponsorship is not available for this role.    A Working with Children Check is   required   for all positions. If successful, we will guide you through the process and reimburse you.    Please upload your resume and a cover letter outlining your interest and experience as part of the application process.    Please upload your responses to the Selection Criteria, found in the Position Description.   Want to know more?   For queries related to this specific position, contact   Nathan Anderson at   nathan.anderson@unimelb.edu.au     For questions related to our recruitment process email   Oliver Bukasa at   hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au   For recruitment adjustments contact Kim Groizard on +61 3 9035 3218 or at   hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au   (subject: 'Recruitment Adjustments').      Apply   today, and   join a community   that’s   shaping the future.   Applications close:  24 September   2026 at   11:55 PM; Melbourne time zone.    Position Description:     JR-018015 - Assistant Farm Hand - PD.docx JR-018015 - Assistant Farm Hand - PD.pdf"
    },
    "https://unimelb.wd105.myworkdayjobs.com/UoM_External_Career/job/Parkville/Student-Operations-Officer_JR-014676-1": {
      "title": "Student Operations Officer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-09\nPosted: Posted 5 Days Ago\nVariable time\n\nRole type:  Part-time (0.4-0.6FTE); Fixed term for 2 years Faculty: Engineering & Information Technology Salary: UoM 5 - $86,943 - $99,864 p.a. plus 17% super   Hands-on makerspace and workshop role / build real-world operational and customer service skills / flexible part-time student position Apply your University studies in a real makerspace environment and help peers learn safely and effectively. Investing in you – 17% superannuation, benefits package including salary packaging, health and wellbeing programs, discounted services, and professional development opportunities.  The University of Melbourne   We take pride in our people, who all contribute to our mission to benefit society through the transformative impact of education and research. Discover more via our website. Your next career opportunity   In this part-time role, you will support safe, hands-on learning in FEIT’s makerspaces and student spaces. You will gain practical operations, customer service and safety experience that complements your University studies. What you will deliver:   Support daily operations of workshops, makerspaces and informal student spaces, ensuring safe, accessible and efficient use. Provide front-line assistance, answering enquiries and guiding users to appropriate training, tools and processes. Deliver inductions and general makerspace training that build user capability and model safe work practices. Assist students, project subjects and clubs with equipment use, budgeting, procurement and basic risk assessments. Contribute to equipment checks, consumable management and process improvements that keep spaces reliable and welcoming. You may be a great fit if you:   Are a current University of Melbourne coursework student with capacity for part-time work during business hours. Bring strong interpersonal, written and verbal communication skills to collaborate with diverse students and staff. Demonstrate a customer service mindset and experience delivering high quality support in busy environments. Show enthusiasm for safe, hands-on work with tools, equipment and technical spaces such as makerspaces or laboratories. Display a growth mindset, contributing constructive ideas to improve processes, user experience and safety practices. Hold or be willing to obtain a valid Employee Working with Children Check for Victoria. For further information please refer to the attached PD.  What we offer you!   We offer the opportunity to be part of a vibrant community and enjoy a comprehensive range of benefits to support your success and sense of fulfilment, including:  Build future financial security with 17% superannuation Supportive flexible work arrangements underpinned by our commitment to inclusion and well-being  Career development opportunities, including access to a range of tailored programs, such as Academic Women in Leadership, and learning platforms including LinkedIn Learning Progressive, considerate leave provisions to empower your work-life balance and well-being, including leading parental leave, gender affirmation leave and cultural leave Salary packaging and access to a range of discounted services including Bupa health insurance, and access to unique cultural and recreational benefits such as discounts for the Melbourne Theatre Company  Health and well-being services including a leading Employee Assistance Program  For more information check out our benefits page!  Your new team You will join the Faculty of Engineering and Information Technology’s Infrastructure team, supporting innovative teaching and research. The Workshop, Makerspaces and Engagement team enables safe, high quality, hands-on learning through well run technical spaces. You will work with passionate professionals and students, gaining practical experience in service delivery, operations and improvement. Be Yourself   The University of Melbourne is an Equal Opportunity Employer and a child-safe organisation. The diversity of our community enriches us all, and we are committed to creating an inclusive and fair workplace where everyone is valued, respected, and empowered to succeed. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, identities, and experiences. Discover more about Diversity and Inclusion at UniMelb. We're committed to a barrier-free recruitment process and ongoing workplace support, providing adjustments throughout. We warmly encourage applications from people with disabilities. Learn more about how we support an accessible recruitment process. Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Applicants   We aspire to be the University of choice for Indigenous Australians. Visit our Indigenous staff page to learn more about our investment and support for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander staff.    Indigenous applicants are encouraged to connect with our Indigenous Employment & Development team at korin-korin@unimelb.edu.au . Application essentials: Visit \"apply with us\" to learn more about the process, including tips and FAQs. You must have current valid work rights for Australia. Visa sponsorship is not available for this role. A Working with Children Check is required for all positions. If successful, we will guide you through the process and reimburse you. Please upload your resume and a cover letter outlining your interest and experience as part of the application process. Please upload your responses to the Selection Criteria, found in the Position Description. Want to know more? For questions related to our recruitment process email Brett Verity at hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au For recruitment adjustments contact Kim Groizard on +61 3 9035 3218 or at hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au (subject: 'Recruitment Adjustments'). Apply today, and join a community that’s shaping the future. Position Description JR-014676 Student Operations Officer PD.docx JR-014676 Student Operations Officer PD.pdf"
    },
    "https://unimelb.wd105.myworkdayjobs.com/UoM_External_Career/job/Parkville/Student-Operations-Coordinator_JR-014660-1": {
      "title": "Student Operations Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-09\nPosted: Posted 5 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nRole type:  Full-time; Fixed term for 2 years Faculty: Engineering & Information Technology Salary: UoM 5 - $86,943 - $99,864 p.a. plus 17% super  Central coordinating role across multiple student spaces / enhance hands-on student experience in workshops and makerspaces / join FEIT’s Infrastructure Team Apply to coordinate student operations, helping deliver safe, inclusive and high-quality spaces for FEIT students. Investing in you – 17% superannuation, benefits package including salary packaging, health and wellbeing programs, discounted services, and professional development opportunities.  The University of Melbourne   We take pride in our people, who all contribute to our mission to benefit society through the transformative impact of education and research. Discover more via our website. Your next career opportunity   In this Student Operations Coordinator role, you will coordinate student operations across FEIT workshops and makerspaces. You will streamline rostering, inductions and documentation, helping deliver safe, reliable and inclusive student spaces. What you will deliver:   Coordinate day-to-day activities and rosters for Student Operations Officers to ensure consistent coverage and service. Act as the operational link, sharing priorities, policy updates, incidents and training needs across the operations team. Maintain and improve shift documentation, SOPs and operational reports, capturing service metrics to support continuous improvement. Support scheduling and administration of inductions, workshops and training, including attendance and competency records. Assist with club and event liaison, coordinating makerspace access and supervision for student projects and activities. You may be a great fit if you:   Bring experience working in customer service environments delivering reliable, high-quality support to diverse users. Demonstrate strong interpersonal, verbal and written communication skills for effective coordination and information sharing. Show a growth mindset, contributing practical ideas to improve processes, documentation and student service experiences. Offer proven ability to follow procedures in operational settings, escalating issues and risks appropriately when needed. Hold familiarity with laboratory, workshop or makerspace environments, including basic health and safety practices. Bring experience supporting students or student-focused services, ideally within education or research-intensive organisations. For further information please refer to the attached PD.  What we offer you!   We offer the opportunity to be part of a vibrant community and enjoy a comprehensive range of benefits to support your success and sense of fulfilment, including:  Build future financial security with 17% superannuation Supportive flexible work arrangements underpinned by our commitment to inclusion and well-being  Career development opportunities, including access to a range of tailored programs, such as Academic Women in Leadership, and learning platforms including LinkedIn Learning Progressive, considerate leave provisions to empower your work-life balance and well-being, including leading parental leave, gender affirmation leave and cultural leave Salary packaging and access to a range of discounted services including Bupa health insurance, and access to unique cultural and recreational benefits such as discounts for the Melbourne Theatre Company  Health and well-being services including a leading Employee Assistance Program  For more information check out our benefits page!  Your new team You will join the Faculty of Engineering and Information Technology’s Infrastructure Team, supporting cutting-edge teaching and research spaces. The Workshop, Makerspaces and Engagement Team enables safe, hands-on learning through well-managed workshops, makerspaces and informal student areas. You will collaborate with technical, operational and student-facing colleagues, contributing to consistently excellent user experiences across FEIT. Be Yourself   The University of Melbourne is an Equal Opportunity Employer and a child-safe organisation. The diversity of our community enriches us all, and we are committed to creating an inclusive and fair workplace where everyone is valued, respected, and empowered to succeed. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, identities, and experiences. Discover more about Diversity and Inclusion at UniMelb. We're committed to a barrier-free recruitment process and ongoing workplace support, providing adjustments throughout. We warmly encourage applications from people with disabilities. Learn more about how we support an accessible recruitment process. Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Applicants   We aspire to be the University of choice for Indigenous Australians. Visit our Indigenous staff page to learn more about our investment and support for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander staff.    Indigenous applicants are encouraged to connect with our Indigenous Employment & Development team at korin-korin@unimelb.edu.au . Application essentials: Visit \"apply with us\" to learn more about the process, including tips and FAQs. You must have current valid work rights for Australia. Visa sponsorship is not available for this role. A Working with Children Check is required for all positions. If successful, we will guide you through the process and reimburse you. Please upload your resume and a cover letter outlining your interest and experience as part of the application process. Please upload your responses to the Selection Criteria, found in the Position Description. Want to know more? For questions related to our recruitment process email Brett Verity at hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au For recruitment adjustments contact Kim Groizard on +61 3 9035 3218 or at hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au (subject: 'Recruitment Adjustments'). Apply today, and join a community that’s shaping the future. Position Description JR-014660 Student Operations Coordinator PD.docx JR-014660 Student Operations Coordinator PD.pdf"
    },
    "https://unimelb.wd105.myworkdayjobs.com/UoM_External_Career/job/Parkville/Marketing-Coordinator-AURIN_JR-018062-1": {
      "title": "Marketing Coordinator AURIN",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-09\nPosted: Posted 5 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nRole type:  Full-time; Fixed-term (6 months) Faculty: Architecture, Building and Planning Department :  Australian Urban Research Infrastructure Network (AURIN) Salary: UOM 7; AUD $111,275 - $120,453 p.a. plus 17% super Work on nationally significant urban data infrastructure / collaborate with experts across academia, government and industry / grow advanced digital marketing capabilities Apply now to lead impactful digital marketing that connects AURIN’s data, tools and stories with key decision makers. Investing in you – 17% superannuation, benefits package including salary packaging, health and wellbeing programs, discounted services, and professional development opportunities.  The University of Melbourne   We take pride in our people, who all contribute to our mission to benefit society through the transformative impact of education and research. Discover more via our website. Your next career opportunity   You will drive creative digital content and campaigns that showcase AURIN’s national urban research and data impact. You will collaborate with experts across academia, government and industry to translate complex insights into compelling stories. You will refine versatile skills in content strategy, stakeholder engagement, events and modern marketing technologies. What you will deliver:   Develop and implement integrated marketing and communications plans that grow AURIN’s visibility, engagement and impact. Create, edit and design high-quality digital and print content tailored to diverse research and policy audiences. Curate stories and case studies by interviewing stakeholders, reviewing research outputs and monitoring urban policy developments. Coordinate scheduling and delivery of eNews, social media, website updates and external communications across all channels. Support event planning and delivery for AURIN conferences, workshops and presentations, including contractor and supplier coordination. You may be a great fit if you:   Hold a degree or equivalent experience in communications, marketing or a closely related field. Bring demonstrated experience implementing innovative communications strategies and measurable results across digital channels. Use tools such as HubSpot, StoryChief, Canva, WordPress and Squarespace for content creation and distribution. Demonstrate ability to translate complex research and data into clear, engaging content for specialist and general audiences. Manage stakeholder relationships with data custodians, researchers and partners, ensuring accurate approvals and high-quality correspondence. Coordinate multiple projects, events and external contractors, maintaining strong customer service and confident internal presentations. For further information please refer to the attached PD.  What we offer you!   We offer the opportunity to be part of a vibrant community and enjoy a comprehensive range of benefits to support your success and sense of fulfilment, including:  Build future financial security with 17% superannuation Supportive flexible work arrangements underpinned by our commitment to inclusion and well-being  Career development opportunities, including access to a range of tailored programs, such as Academic Women in Leadership, and learning platforms including LinkedIn Learning Progressive, considerate leave provisions to empower your work-life balance and well-being, including leading parental leave, gender affirmation leave and cultural leave Salary packaging and access to a range of discounted services including Bupa health insurance, and access to unique cultural and recreational benefits such as discounts for the Melbourne Theatre Company  Health and well-being services including a leading Employee Assistance Program  For more information check out our benefits page!  Your new team At AURIN in the Faculty of Architecture, Building and Planning, you will join a small marketing team. The team is collaborative, works fluidly and manages complex moving parts with autonomy and confidence. You will partner with leading academics, government and industry to apply geospatial and urban data for better cities. Be Yourself   The University of Melbourne is an Equal Opportunity Employer and a child-safe organisation. The diversity of our community enriches us all, and we are committed to creating an inclusive and fair workplace where everyone is valued, respected, and empowered to succeed. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, identities, and experiences. Discover more about Diversity and Inclusion at UniMelb. We're committed to a barrier-free recruitment process and ongoing workplace support, providing adjustments throughout. We warmly encourage applications from people with disabilities. Learn more about how we support an accessible recruitment process. Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Applicants   We aspire to be the University of choice for Indigenous Australians. Visit our Indigenous staff page to learn more about our investment and support for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander staff.    Indigenous applicants are encouraged to connect with our Indigenous Employment & Development team at korin-korin@unimelb.edu.au . Application essentials: Visit \"apply with us\" to learn more about the process, including tips and FAQs. You must have current valid work rights for Australia. Visa sponsorship is not available for this role. A Working with Children Check is required for all positions. If successful, we will guide you through the process and reimburse you. Please upload your resume and a cover letter outlining your interest and experience as part of the application process. Please upload your responses to the Selection Criteria, found in the Position Description. Want to know more? For questions related to our recruitment process email Brett Verity at hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au For recruitment adjustments contact Kim Groizard on +61 3 9035 3218 or at hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au (subject: 'Recruitment Adjustments'). Apply today, and join a community that’s shaping the future. Position Description JR-018062 Marketing Coordinator AURIN PD.docx JR-018062 Marketing Coordinator AURIN PD.pdf"
    },
    "https://unimelb.wd105.myworkdayjobs.com/UoM_External_Career/job/Parkville-Victoria/Early-Childhood-Educator---Diploma--Part-time-_JR-017604-1": {
      "title": "Early Childhood Educator - Diploma (Part time)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-08\nPosted: Posted 6 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nRole type:   Part- time   (0. 4 4   FTE) ;   Continuing     Department / School:   Student and Scholarly Services; Chancellery Education Portfolio    Salary:   $ 80,400 - 85,328 p.a.   (pro rata for part- time)   plu s   17% super    Deliver high-quality, play-based programmes / work within supportive university early childhood centres / grow your   expertise   across age groups   Join our Early Childhood Education Services team and help shape exceptional learning and care for children.   Investing in you – 17% superannuation, benefits package including salary packaging, health and wellbeing programs, discounted services, and professional development opportunities.      The University of Melbourne     We take pride in our people, who all contribute to our mission to   benefit   society through the transformative impact of education and research.   Discover more via our website.   Your next career opportunity     In this role, you will design and deliver high-quality programmes for children aged three months to five years.   You will collaborate with a committed team across three centres, continuously enhancing practice under the National Quality Framework.   You will mentor colleagues, document learning meaningfully, and champion inclusive, child-led environments that nurture agency and wellbeing.   What you will deliver:     Implement and evaluate inclusive, play-based programmes aligned with EYLF, VEYLDF and National Quality Framework requirements.   Supervise children to ensure safety and wellbeing,   maintaining   accurate   records and observations that inform responsive programme planning.   Design and   maintain   sensory-rich, aesthetically pleasing learning environments that challenge, extend and support children’s play and development.   Build respectful, inclusive relationships with families and colleagues, sharing insights and updates on children’s needs,   progress   and programmes.   Contribute to centre Quality Improvement planning, mentoring educators and, when   required , acting as Responsible Person in leadership’s absence.       You may be a great fit   if   you :     Hold an ACECQA-approved Diploma qualification, current WWCC, HLTAID012 First Aid, and   required   child safety and food safety training.   Bring at least two years’ experience in early childhood education across multiple age groups and service types.   Demonstrate   expertise   designing,   implementing   and evaluating programmes aligned with EYLF, VEYLDF and National Quality Standards regulatory frameworks.   Apply strong knowledge of relevant legislation, including Education and Care National Law, Child Safe   Standards   and privacy obligations.   Offer experience supervising and mentoring educators or students, providing constructive feedback and supporting continuous pedagogical improvement.   Utilise sound IT skills and clear English communication to produce high-quality documentation that   evidences   children’s learning and progress.   For further   information   please refer to the attached PD.    What we offer you!     We offer the opportunity to be part of a vibrant community and enjoy a comprehensive range of benefits to support your success and sense of fulfilment, including:    Build future financial security with 17% superannuation   Supportive flexible work arrangements underpinned by our commitment to inclusion and well-being    Career development opportunities, including access to a range of tailored programs, such as Academic Women in Leadership, and learning platforms including LinkedIn Learning   Progressive, considerate leave provisions to empower your work-life balance and well-being, including leading parental leave, gender affirmation leave and cultural leave   Salary packaging and access to a range of discounted services including Bupa health insurance, and access to unique cultural and recreational benefits such as discounts for the Melbourne Theatre Company    Health and well-being services including a leading Employee Assistance Program    For more information check out our benefits page!     Your new team :   Early Childhood Education Services is a vibrant, child-centred service within Student and Scholarly Services.   Across three centres, our team supports around 350 children from the University and wider community.   We are a collaborative group of around 60 educators, teachers and leaders committed to excellence.   We embrace contemporary early childhood pedagogy, reflective   practice   and sector-leading compliance with the National Quality Framework.   We value inclusion,   respect   and professional growth, offering rich opportunities to develop your   expertise   across age groups.   Be Yourself     The   University of Melbourne is an Equal Opportunity Employer and a child-safe   organisation . The diversity of our community enriches us all, and we are committed to creating an inclusive and fair workplace where everyone is valued, respected, and empowered to succeed. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, identities, and experiences.   Discover more about Diversity and Inclusion at UniMelb.   We're   committed to a barrier-free recruitment process and ongoing workplace support, providing adjustments throughout. We warmly encourage applications from people with disabilities.   Learn more about how we support an accessible recruitment process .   Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Applicants     We aspire to be the University of choice for Indigenous Australians.   Visit   our   Indigenous staff page   to learn more about our investment and support for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander staff.            Indigenous applicants are encouraged to connect with our Indigenous Employment & Development team at   korin-korin@unimelb.edu.au .    Application essentials:   Visit   \"apply with us\"   to learn more about the process, including tips and FAQs.   You must have current valid work rights for Australia. Visa sponsorship is not available for this role.    A Working with Children Check is   required   for all positions. If successful, we will guide you through the process and reimburse you.    Please upload your resume and a cover letter outlining your interest and experience as part of the application process.    Please upload your responses to the   Essential   Selection Criteria, found in the Position Description.    Want to know more?   For questions related to our recruitment process email  Alex Spezza at   hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au   For recruitment adjustments contact Kim Groizard on +61 3 9035 3218 or at   hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au   (subject: 'Recruitment Adjustments').    Apply   today, and   join a community   that’s   shaping the future.   Applications close:  Sunday 20th of September 2026   11:55 PM; Melbourne time zone.    Position Description:     JR-017604 Early Childhood Educator - Diploma (Part time) - PD.docx JR-017604 Early Childhood Educator - Diploma (Part time) - PD.pdf"
    },
    "https://unimelb.wd105.myworkdayjobs.com/UoM_External_Career/job/Parkville/Subject-Coordinator---Master-of-Counselling_JR-017886": {
      "title": "Subject Coordinator - Master of Counselling",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-08\nPosted: Posted 6 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nRole type: Full-time; Fixed term for 2 years   Faculty: Medicine, Dentistry and Health Sciences   Department/School: School of Health Sciences – Department of Social Work   Salary: Level B - $124,656 - $148,023 p.a. plus 17% super     Pioneering new online Master of Counselling / Lead curriculum and subject development / Collaborate with expert multidisciplinary educators     Join us to design, coordinate and teach innovative online counselling subjects that build future-ready practitioners.   Investing in you – 17% superannuation, benefits package including salary packaging, health and wellbeing programs, discounted services, and professional development opportunities.     The University of Melbourne   We take pride in our people, who all contribute to our mission to benefit society through the transformative impact of education and research. Discover more via our website.   Your next career opportunity:   You will shape curriculum and subjects for a new fully online Master of Counselling launching in 2026 .You will teach and coordinate online subjects, and support educators to deliver engaging, practice-relevant learning experiences.   What you will deliver:   Design and refine online Master of Counselling curriculum in partnership with academic leaders and Melbourne Online specialists.   Develop, coordinate and review online subject content, ensuring high quality, coherent learning experiences across the degree.   Teach counselling subjects online and supervise, mentor and support online educators contributing to the program.   Ensure subject delivery, assessment and academic integrity comply with departmental, University and professional accreditation requirements.   Contribute to departmental governance, planning, policy development and community partnerships that strengthen the program’s impact.     You may be a great fit if you:   Hold a Master of Counselling or equivalent and meet eligibility requirements for ACA membership.   Bring experience designing and developing counselling, social work or human services curricula, particularly for online delivery.   Demonstrate successful teaching and coordination of counselling subjects, with evidence of innovation and flexibility in online modes.   Exhibit strong organisational skills, managing multiple tasks and deadlines while maintaining high academic and service standards.   Build effective relationships with diverse stakeholders, collaborating to achieve shared program and departmental goals.   Show clear commitment to equity, diversity, inclusion and reconciliation within teaching, curriculum and professional practice .   For further information please refer to the attached PD.    What we offer you!   We offer the opportunity to be part of a vibrant community and enjoy a comprehensive range of benefits to support your success and sense of fulfilment, including:    Build future financial security with 17% superannuation   Supportive flexible work arrangements underpinned by our commitment to inclusion and well-being    Career development opportunities, including access to a range of tailored programs, such as Academic Women in Leadership, and learning platforms including LinkedIn Learning   Progressive, considerate leave provisions to empower your work-life balance and well-being, including leading parental leave, gender affirmation leave and cultural leave   Salary packaging and access to a range of discounted services including Bupa health insurance, and access to unique cultural and recreational benefits such as discounts for the Melbourne Theatre Company    Health and well-being services including a leading Employee Assistance Program    For more information check out our benefits page!   Your new team – “ Department of Social Work ”   You will join the Department of Social Work within the School of Health Sciences, a recognised regional leader. The department has a strong research profile and deep partnerships with government, non- government and professional human service agencies.   Our team delivers innovative on-campus and online programmes, including advanced social work and human services qualifications. You will collaborate with experienced educators and Melbourne Online specialists to shape a new flagship Master of Counselling.     Be Yourself   The University of Melbourne is an Equal Opportunity Employer and a child-safe organisation. The diversity of our community enriches us all, and we are committed to creating an inclusive and fair workplace where everyone is valued, respected, and empowered to succeed. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, identities, and experiences. Discover more about Diversity and Inclusion at UniMelb .   We're committed to a barrier-free recruitment process and ongoing workplace support, providing adjustments throughout. We warmly encourage applications from people with disabilities. Learn more about how we support an accessible recruitment process .   Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Applicants   We aspire to be the University of choice for Indigenous Australians. Visit our Indigenous staff page to learn more about our investment and support for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander staff.        Indigenous applicants are encouraged to connect with our Indigenous Employment & Development team at korin-korin@unimelb.edu.au .    Application essentials:   Visit \"apply with us\" to learn more about the process, including tips and FAQs.   You must have current valid work rights for Australia. Visa sponsorship is not available for this role..   A Working with Children Check is required for all positions. If successful, we will guide you through the process and reimburse you.    Please upload your resume and a cover letter outlining your interest and experience as part of the application process.    Please upload your responses to the Selection Criteria, found in the Position Description.      Want to know more?   For questions related to our recruitment process email hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au   For recruitment adjustments contact Kim Groizard on +61 3 9035 3218 or at hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au (subject: 'Recruitment Adjustments').    Apply today, and join a community that’s shaping the future.   Applications close: Tuesday 22 September at 11:55 PM; Melbourne time zone.    Position Description: PD Subject Coordinator M Counselling.docx   PD Subject Coordinator M Counselling.pdf"
